From 9a3fd09d21d617921cb0d4dba088a9c7548302a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 05:12:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Keep a player's tag by name, so it survives their zoning,
 camping and dying

Saved tags were keyed by zone and spawn id, which only works for NPCs. A
player gets a new spawn id every time they zone in, so a tagged player
who zoned out and back, or who zoned with you, came back untagged. Worse,
if they left and returned while you stayed in the zone, the saved tag was
still marked as seen live, so the untagged newcomer read as a clear and
the saved tag was deleted.

Player names are unique on the server, so:

- Players are saved in their own map, keyed by stripped name and not tied
  to a zone. The tag comes back when they return after zoning, camping or
  dying (their corpse neither takes it nor drops it), and follows them
  into another zone with you.
- handle_entity_destructor marks a leaving player's saved tag as not live,
  so their return restores it instead of clearing it.
- Clearing a tag on a player in view still drops it. A clear drops every
  player tag, since they belong to no zone. Player tags expire 3 hours
  after the player was last seen, like the rest.
- The tag file gains player lines: zone -1, spawn id 0, then the name.
  Older builds never match zone -1, so a shared file stays harmless.
- NPC rules are unchanged; the shared save/restore steps moved into one
  lambda that both maps use.
- README: note player tags.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Uq6P6RYLtiKKfy5UWjT7AX
